During the 1971–72 Scottish football season, [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] competed in [[Scottish Division One]]. Celtic won the Scottish League for the seventh time in a row, a record at the time. They also successfully retained the [[Scottish Cup]]. This was the seventh season in a row in which Celtic won at least two of the three major domestic honours in Scotland (League, Cup and League Cup), a record that has not been broken or equalled as of 2025.

